0..55 Comment "//! Completion handles an overlap that parts at a call."
56..59 Comment "//!"
60..112 Comment "//! The two `swap` rules overlap at `swap(Zero, n)`."
113..116 Comment "//!"
117..175 Comment "//! One reduct is `n`. The other reduct is `add(n, Zero)`."
176..256 Comment "//! Completion derives a rule from `add(n, Zero)` to `n`. The derived rule joins"
257..314 Comment "//! the pair. The kernel reads it with the written rules."
315..318 Comment "//!"
319..334 Comment "//! - see: #338"
335..400 Comment "//! - cites: [Knuth-1970-simple_word_problems_universal_algebras]"
401..404 Comment "//!"
405..576 Comment "//! [Knuth-1970-simple_word_problems_universal_algebras]: https://doi.org/10.1016/B978-0-08-012975-4.50028-X \"Knuth and Bendix, Simple Word Problems in Universal Algebras\""
